This file contains current priorities.

COMBAT REWORK:
- Projectile Functionality
- Damage and destroy objects
- Custom object destruction results & configurable particles
- Entity damage
- A seamless system of hit detection > damage/other effects
- Configured SFX
- "Weapons" & Attacks functionality
- Fix normalizeAttacks in core/normalize.js: the .map callback has no return, so every entity's attacks array is the right length and entirely undefined
Option to block scatter spawn on top of decals
- Add spikes to Carl model
Entity AI:
- Default behaviours (not mutually exclusive):
  - Chase
  - Search
  - Idle
  - Wander
  - Guard
  - Attack
  - Defend
- Custom behaviours: Game attaches handlers OR events.
Player Abilities:
- Pretty much have to be custom handlers. Optional use, game can choose to apply effects manually.
- Maybe some standards? Like double jump? Boosting?
Ledge balancing: partial rotation at an edge already reads as leaning — build it into an almost-falling state.
Rework Collectible system into collections with built-in handling support.
Build new trigger types:
- Only camera triggers do anything today; custom, dialogue and cutscene validate and fire no events.
- Level Clear
- Custom
- Teleport
Add new Terrain, Obstacle and Entity Templates.
- Think of a list with Claude
- Sonic-style Loop (Terrain)
- Half-Pipe (Terrain)
- City Rubble (Obstacle)
- Basketball Hoop (Obstacle)
- Shrine (Terrain)
Build Load Screen functionality.
- Background Image support
- HTML Element support
- Music Support
Add aliases to canonSchemas.json
Performance Enhancements (DRYAD):
- Must abide simulation distance:
  - Any animations. From textures to entities.
  - Runtime instance spawning. Any instance that's being spawned too far, gets enqueued until the player gets close enough.


Additions to Level API:
- Entities:
  - GetState(entityId)
  - GetAll
  - Animate(entityId, ...)
  - Kill(entityId)
  - Delete(entityId)
  - Heal(entityId, amount)
  - SetPhysics(entityId, ...)
  - SetMeta(entityId, ...)
  - SetPosition(entityId)
  - SetScale(entityId)
  - Damage(objectType, id, amount)
  - SetAction(entityId, ...)
  - SetNpcBehavior(entityId, ...)
  - NpcAccessories
- Player:
  - Animate
  - CharacterSwitch
  - SetPosition
  - SetScale
  - SetMeta
  - SetAction
  - Kill
  - Heal
  - Damage
  - Launch(velocity) — sets velocity and the `launched` flag together, so games can make the player lose their footing.
  - Accessories
  - GetState
- Spawn:
  - Terrain
  - Obstacle
  - Entity
  - Trigger
- Camera:
  - Switch
  - SetPosition
  - GetPosition
  - GetDirection — aim-where-you-look needs camera forward; today it's GetActiveLevel().cameraConfig.state.forward.
  - Snapshot
- Trigger(triggerId)
- Do:
  -
- GetSnapshot
- Per-frame hook (callback or LEVEL_TICK), so games stop running their own rAF loop one frame out of phase with the sim.
- IsPaused()
- LEVEL_PAUSED carries its source (player vs PauseLevel()), so a game-over freeze doesn't need a game-side flag.


Add full documentation API so devs can understand how to work the engine.


Create a level interpreter that reads level json data and returns 2D representations of the level.
- The output can be ASCII/data (for AI)
- The output can be JPEGs
- Output can be multiple. Things stacked on top of each other are hard to define, so each piece of output should reflect a height region based on the height differences in objects (aka dynamic)


Allow special rotational control so Carl can rotate in water with Q and E
- Line up to things you want to attach to.
- A and D controls change direction.


Version Goals:
- 0.32: Main Update Released [FINISHED]
- 0.33: Decal Rework [FINISHED]
  1. Pre-load Simulator Cache with player-characters and all templates. [DONE]
  2. Jump Window Expansion (ground probe so early presses can register early; tiny window after losing ground contact) [DONE]
    - Make rendering obey FrameRate. [DONE]
  3. Sticky Terrain: [DONE]
    - Fix bug where you clip out of bounds in voids. [DONE]
    - Add a "sticky" field to terrain. The player's grounding is no longer tied to a minimum speed while grounded on this part. [DONE]
- 0.34: Camera & Controls Stability [FINISHED]
    - Offset the camera at incline changes so it remains vertically stationary during loops. Ensure it doesn't influence movement. [DONE]
  1. Loop detection false positives [DONE]
    - The upward slope in the tunnel connecting underwater and above water counts as a loop, forcing a bad side-view camera angle.
  2. Backface Culling [DONE]
    - Fix Water vs Trigger layering. [DONE]
  3.  Toon-switch for outlines. [DONE]
  4. DEFERRED Performance Enhancements [DONE]
    - Move Render.js Shaders to new Shaders.js module. [DONE]
    - Move Object.js shape functions to new NewPrimitive.js module. [DONE]
      - Center the pyramid: its base sits at y=0, so the bottom-center lift floats it by half its height. Carl has pyramid-hosted decals, so check him after. [DONE]
  5. FrameRate Coercion [DONE]
  6. Todo Performance Enhancements [DONE]
- 0.35 Occlusion Culling & CPU Optimizations [CURRENT]
    - Built: blocker culling in Render.js hideOccluded, helpers in math/Collision.js, occluder records from NewTerrain.js. ARGUS: 0 false hides on lvl2, stress grid, LSM. Scope: docs/scoping/render/culling-scope.md §4.5.
    - Left: remove testGame lvlStress.json and its level.js entry.
  1. orbitCam Rework [PENDING]
    - Games can't set the initial camera yaw or the player's spawn facing (LSM rotated its whole level 180° to work around it).
    - Mouse sensitivity is read once at level start, so a settings change mid-level does nothing until the next level.
  2. Sprite/Bilboard Support (rotating images that resize based on distance)
    - Look into adding mipmaps to remove the weird rounded artifacts at a distance.
  3. Movement Enhancements. [PENDING]
    - Release jump early for quicker falloff.
    - Solve over-rotation in above-water tunnel.
    - Store medium (Water/Air) on entity definition (e.g. playerState)
    - If holding "A", then pressing and releasing "D", "A" stops working until it's pressed again. This must be fixed.
    - Jumping off a sloped surface doesn't feel correct because you keep so much upwards momentum. It can feel like you're still jumping "up" while you're rotated 80 degrees, which is not how jumping should feel.
  4. Look into why moving and running through voids causes performance drops.
- 0.36: Workers (Multi-Threading) [PENDING]
  - Needs a full scoping pass.
  - Consider a coordinator/state manager. If small, an exported "Workforce" object in meta.js acting as the state manager could work quite well. It'd check if workers are available and assign them.
  - Candidates for Worker Tasks:
    - Build-time Texture generation/baking (lvl2 water face bake is ~1.3/~3.4s of the load time). Speeds up level build.
      - Could contain runtime noise-rebaking. Candidate for permanent worker slot.
    - Entity Pathfinding (0.36). Candidate for a permanent worker slot (cannot be assigned to other tasks).
    - think of more candidates just in case...
- 0.37: Primitive Expansion
  - Options:
    - "rounding" & "complexity" to Cubes
    - "domeRatio" to Spheres
  - Shapes:
    - "diamond" (complexity makes it range from a jewel to something more like a nose)
  - Expand Instance.js to reduce tedious json authoring. Add missing fields. No datatype normalization.
    - Remove dead fields in Engine json.
    - Update engine rule docs.
  - Move more non-standard fields to primitiveOptions
  - Look into unifying capsule and cylinder.
    - Add "topRounding" and "bottomRounding" primitiveOptions, which equate to how much of the cylinder the cap replaces.
  1. Allow voids on entities (they'll act as carving). Void walls must start supporting decals.
- 0.38: Entity AI
  - Blueprint movement fields chase, jump, jumpOnSight, disappear and aggroRange validate but do nothing; devs read them as the AI API.
  - Make SimRadius a calculation rather than authorable.
    - Entities will replace velocity with velocity.start, and gain velocity.max (including the player, losing maxSpeed)
    - SimRadius will equal: (velocity.max / 10) * (60 / CONFIG.Performance.FrameRate)
    - Double SimRadius for the player
    - SimRadius is in CNU. velocity.max is CNU/s
  1. Add optional Q/W rotation controls & add full custom player controls support.
  2. Add optional Swimming & Flying states.
  3. Add player/characters.json animation authoring support.
  x. Bug fixes.
- 0.39: Additional Control Schemes
  - Controller Support.
  - Custom control bindings.
    - Add gameplay controls bindings to API_CONFIG so games don't have to run custom event listeners (they still can if they want).
      - Standard movement and camera controls have defaults.
      - Any abilities for the player authored in the level payload are added as extra properties for authoring in the config (needs a function that also emits logs for added and removed API fields).
      - Any of these can be changed to "none" and the engine stops listening for those.
      - A full 
      - The Simulator has a hardcoded controls scheme.
  - Input magnitude is ignored: Movement normalizes the direction, so forward: 0.5 is full speed. Analog sticks need it.
  - No invert-Y option.
- 0.40: Combat Expansion
  - Player hp is a stale 3 nothing reads; damage is ring rules only. Games build hearts/HP/i-frames themselves.
  - One enemy hit soft-locks the player: Stunned and invulnerable are set, but nothing counts the timer down or leaves Stunned before respawn.
  x. Bug fixes.
- 0.41: Collectible Rework
  1. Bug fixes.
  2. Increase game-side control in sub-systems.
  3. Load Screen functionality.
- 0.42: Abilities Support:
  - Standard simple abilities.
  - Player.Input.boost is read by nothing, and nothing sets playerState.boost.active. LSM wrote GetState().boost directly for sprint.
  - 
- 0.43: Moving Terrain & Obstacles.
  - Moving terrain gets no occlusion blocker pieces (static-only blocking is permanent); it can still be hidden.
- 0.44: DEFERRED Backlog Cleanup
  1. Optionally block scatter on decals.
  2. Add scatter support to voids.
  3. Block scatter inside objects.
    - Block generation if cheaper than post-generation block.
    - Mark for runtime culling for moving platforms.
  4. ApplyLevelUI [PENDING]
    - ApplyMenuUI becomes strictly non-level menus that replace each other.
    - ApplyLevelUI layers in-level UI (HUDs, inventories, pause menus, tooltips) on top of each other, optionally pausing gameplay while open. Shares most logic with ApplyMenuUI.
    - Complaint: ApplyMenuUI mid-level resets the input event types, killing mouse look, wheel and arrow look until pause/resume. HUDs had to be applied before CreateLevel with every later element pre-built and hidden.
    - Complaint: no way to update an element's text or style; live HUD values go through document.getElementById.
  5. Level Music Playlist [PENDING]
    - Level music block gains "start", "loop" and "shuffle".
      - start: optional track, always the first to play when the level starts.
      - loop: array of tracks played one after another after start, looping forever.
      - shuffle: picks loop tracks at random; the same track never plays twice in a row unless loop holds only one.
    - Complaint: level music was validated and normalized but never played; testGame plays it itself after CreateLevel, and nothing pauses it with the level.
